WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT A LICENSE FILE

  Download, integrate and evaluate the SDK with no time limit, on device and in
  the simulator. Every feature renders. An unlicensed app shows a small badge
  over the rendered content and logs one console warning; nothing is withheld
  and nothing stops working.

WHAT A LICENSE FILE ADDS

  Removing that badge. A license is issued after purchase at
  https://macdeer.com/pricing, is bound to your Apple Developer Team ID, and
  covers every app that team signs — including apps you create later. It is
  verified offline on device and sends no network request.

  A license does not expire by date. It names an update window: builds of this
  SDK released within that window may be used indefinitely in your apps. Using
  builds released after the window ends requires renewing the update service.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

  Redistribute, resell, publish, mirror, rent or sublicense the SDK itself,
  including as part of a source bundle, template or starter kit. Integrating it
  into your own application and shipping that application is exactly what the
  license is for; shipping the SDK as something someone else can take out and
  use is not.

  Remove, disable, obscure or circumvent the license verification or the
  unlicensed badge, or modify the binary to that end.

  Reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the framework, except to the
  extent that applicable law expressly permits it despite this restriction.

